          "lem-qft-free-domain-observables",
          "lem-qft-scalar-local-weyl-algebra",
          "lem-qft-free-dirac-car-locality",
          "thm-dominated-convergence"
        ],
        "dependency_roles": {
          "def-qft-framework-units": "formulation-prerequisite",
          "def-countable-choice": "mathematical-premise",
          "post-qft-free-field-model": "physical-assumption",
          "post-qft-constructed-model-and-measurement": "physical-assumption",
          "def-qft-free-field-observables": "formulation-prerequisite",
          "lem-qft-free-domain-observables": "mathematical-premise",
          "lem-qft-scalar-local-weyl-algebra": "mathematical-premise",
          "lem-qft-free-dirac-car-locality": "mathematical-premise",
          "thm-dominated-convergence": "mathematical-premise"
        },
        "physical_scope": "The selected flat four-dimensional real scalar bosonic and Dirac CAR Fock models, with their chosen vacua and bounded smeared observable algebras. Operator-domain and point-smearing conclusions are conditional on the named mathematical carriers. No interacting theory, pointwise field operator, coincident product, thermal trace, apparatus, or empirical outcome is asserted.",
        "empirical_premises": [],
        "statement": "Assume Countable Choice, $\\mu\\ge0$, and the selected free-field model of\n[[post-qft-free-field-model]]. Use the four-dimensional affine Minkowski chart,\nsignature $\\eta=\\operatorname{diag}(-1,1,1,1)$, length coordinate $x^0=ct$,\nand inverse-length parameter $\\mu$ of [[def-qft-framework-units]]. For an open\nregion $O\\subseteq\\mathbb R^4$, use the scalar and Dirac test functions and\nbounded local observable algebras defined in\n[[def-qft-free-field-observables]]: scalar tests are real members of\n$C_c^\\infty(O)$, Dirac tests are members of\n$C_c^\\infty(O;\\mathbb C^4)$, and the Dirac observable algebra is generated by\neven products of bounded smeared CAR fields and their adjoints.\n\nFor a real Schwartz scalar test $f$, the closure of $\\Phi_\\mu(f)$ is\nself-adjoint on its exact Segal-field multiplier domain. The scalar number,\nHamiltonian and momentum operators and the Dirac Hamiltonian and momentum\noperators have the exact maximal sector-sum domains stated in\n[[lem-qft-free-domain-observables]]. In particular,\n$$D(N_s)=\\left\\{\\Psi=(\\Psi_n):\\sum_{n\\ge1}n^2\\|\\Psi_n\\|^2<\\infty\\right\\}.$$\nIf $A$ is one of these self-adjoint operators and $\\Psi$ is normalized with\n$\\Psi\\in D(A)$, then its model mean $\\langle\\Psi,A\\Psi\\rangle$ and variance\n$$\\operatorname{Var}_\\Psi(A)=\\|(A-\\langle\\Psi,A\\Psi\\rangle)\\Psi\\|^2$$\nare finite; this needs $\\Psi\\in D(A)$, not $\\Psi\\in D(A^2)$. The product\n$AB\\Psi$ is defined only when $\\Psi\\in D(B)$ and $B\\Psi\\in D(A)$.\n\nIf $O_1,O_2$ are open regions and\n$\\eta_{ab}(x-y)^a(x-y)^b>0$ for every $x\\in O_1$ and $y\\in O_2$, then the\nscalar Weyl algebras of the two regions commute, and the even local Dirac\nalgebras of the two regions commute. These are algebraic properties of the\nspecified free representations.\n\nThe chosen construction supplies only test-smeared fields and does not define\n$\\Phi_\\mu(x)$, $\\Psi(x)$, or coincident diagonal products. Fix a point\n$x_0\\in\\mathbb R^4$ and a nonnegative normalized Schwartz Gaussian\n$\\rho\\in\\mathscr S(\\mathbb R^4)$, and put\n$\\rho_{\\epsilon,x_0}(x)=\\epsilon^{-4}\\rho((x-x_0)/\\epsilon)$. These tests\napproximate $\\delta_{x_0}$ on Schwartz functions, but\n$\\|\\Phi_\\mu(\\rho_{\\epsilon,x_0})\\Omega\\|\\to\\infty$ as $\\epsilon\\downarrow0$.\nFor an equal-time Dirac field, fix a unit spinor $z$ and a nonnegative\nnormalized Schwartz Gaussian $\\sigma$ on $\\mathbb R^3$, and put\n$u_{\\epsilon,x_0}(\\mathbf x)=\\epsilon^{-3}\n\\sigma((\\mathbf x-\\mathbf x_0)/\\epsilon)z$. These tests approximate a\nspatial point mass, while $\\|\\Psi_t(u_{\\epsilon,x_0})\\|\\to\\infty$. Neither\nfamily has a finite limit in its respective Fock or operator-norm topology.\nThis restriction does not rule out other distributional or renormalized\nconstructions. The Born interpretation of\n[[post-qft-constructed-model-and-measurement]] applies only after a density\nstate and normalized finite bounded instrument have actually been supplied;\nthis item reports no apparatus or outcome.",
        "proof_strategy": "direct",
        "provenance": {
          "statement": "literature-derived",
          "proof": "ai-altered"
        },
        "sources": {
          "references": [
            {
