      {
        "id": "pthm-qft-classical-quantum-free-correspondence",
        "kind": "physics-theorem",
        "domain": "physics",
        "title": "Classical equations and adopted exact free quantum representation",
        "reference": "research/extended-frameworks-2026-10-03/quantum-field-theory/proposed-inventory.json#QFT-F04",
        "design_state": "Checks the classical compact-variation scalar and Dirac equations against the tested equations of the separately adopted free representations. Quantization and statistics assignments are model assumptions, not deductions from the classical actions.",
        "dependency_level": 7,
        "deps": [
          "def-qft-framework-units",
          "def-countable-choice",
          "post-qft-free-field-model",
          "lem-qft-free-action-equations",
          "lem-qft-mass-shell-test-restriction-continuity",
          "lem-qft-smeared-free-scalar",
          "lem-qft-free-dirac-car-locality"
        ],
        "dependency_roles": {
          "def-qft-framework-units": "formulation-prerequisite",
          "def-countable-choice": "mathematical-premise",
          "post-qft-free-field-model": "physical-assumption",
          "lem-qft-free-action-equations": "mathematical-premise",
          "lem-qft-mass-shell-test-restriction-continuity": "mathematical-premise",
          "lem-qft-smeared-free-scalar": "mathematical-premise",
          "lem-qft-free-dirac-car-locality": "mathematical-premise"
        },
        "physical_scope": "The selected flat four-dimensional free real scalar and Dirac models, with the stated (-+++) signature, inverse-length mass parameter and chosen Fock representations. The result matches compact-variation classical equations with weak test equations of the adopted representations. It does not derive quantization, a general spin-statistics rule, interacting dynamics, empirical validity, or a measurement outcome.",
        "empirical_premises": [],
        "statement": "Assume Countable Choice and the selected free-field model of\n[[post-qft-free-field-model]], using the metric, length coordinates, inverse-\nlength parameter $\\mu\\ge0$, field dimensions and Clifford convention fixed by\n[[def-qft-framework-units]]. The classical scalar field\n$\\phi_{\\mathrm n}:\\mathbb R^4\\to\\mathbb R$ is smooth and real; the classical\nDirac field $\\psi_{\\mathrm n}:\\mathbb R^4\\to\\mathbb C^4$ is smooth with\ncommuting components. Their adopted free actions are the scalar and Dirac\nfunctionals stated in [[post-qft-free-field-model]]. Action symbols are used\nonly through compactly supported smooth variations, so no global\nintegrability of the classical background fields is assumed.\n\nThe compact-variation stationarity equations are\n$$(\\Box-\\mu^2)\\phi_{\\mathrm n}=0,\\qquad (i\\gamma^a\\partial_a-\\mu)\\psi_{\\mathrm n}=0,$$\nwith $\\Box=-\\partial_0^2+\\Delta_{\\mathbf x}$. In the separately adopted\nscalar and Dirac Fock representations, the corresponding weak test equations\nare, for $f\\in\\mathscr S(\\mathbb R^4)$ and\n$F\\in\\mathscr S(\\mathbb R^4;\\mathbb C^4)$,\n$$\\Phi_\\mu((\\Box-\\mu^2)f)=0,\\qquad \\Psi\\!\\left((i\\partial_0-h_D(-i\\nabla))F\\right)=0.$$\nHere “weak test equation” means precisely that smearing the constructed field\nwith the displayed differential operator gives the zero operator on its\nstated common domain. With $h_D(\\mathbf k)=\\boldsymbol\\alpha\\cdot\\mathbf k+\\beta\\mu$,\n$\\gamma^0=\\beta$, and $\\gamma^j=\\beta\\alpha^j$ as adopted in\n[[post-qft-free-field-model]], the Dirac test operator is equivalent to\n$i\\gamma^a\\partial_a-\\mu$.\n\nThus the classical action equations and the tested equations of the selected\nfree representations have the same differential expressions at these\nnormalizations. The Fock representation, species/statistics assignments and\nvacua are additional physical model assumptions; they are not deductions from\nthe classical actions. No empirical outcome or measurement is asserted.",
        "proof_strategy": "direct",
        "provenance": {
          "statement": "literature-derived",
          "proof": "ai-altered"
        },
        "sources": {
          "references": [
            {
              "title": "David Tong, Quantum Field Theory, author-hosted complete lecture notes, Chapter 1, §1.1.1",
              "url": "https://www.damtp.cam.ac.uk/user/tong/qft/qfthtml/S1.html",
              "locator": "Complete HTML Chapter 1; §1.1.1, the real scalar action and Klein–Gordon Euler–Lagrange equation."
            },
